  "root_cause": [
    "closed was set before cleanup and also used as its completion guard, so interrupted cleanup became a permanent no-op on subsequent close.",
    "The unconditional finally joined a reader and then closed buffered stdout even when kill/wait failed and the peer could still keep the reader blocked.",
    "close previously only marked closed after adapter.close, allowing same-thread cleanup code to issue another request."
  ],
  "fix": [
    "Keep closed as the immediate request-rejection state; set it before invoking adapter.close, after rejecting active-physics-callback close.",
    "Track _transport_closed separately; set it only after the transport teardown path completes. Repeated close and destructor can retry incomplete cleanup without disposing the detached adapter again.",
    "On a transport cleanup exception, set _broken and re-raise the original exception. Next close attempts kill/reap before closing stdin. No internal retry loop was added.",
    "Only join and close stdout after successful wait; check the reader has stopped before buffered stdout.close. Both normal and post-kill wait use timeout=2, and reader join uses timeout=2."
  ],
